<?php
namespace App\Controller;

use Symfony\Bundle\FrameworkBundle\Controller\AbstractController;
use Symfony\Component\HttpFoundation\Response;
use Symfony\Component\Routing\Attribute\Route;

final class RulesSettingsController extends AbstractController
{
    #[Route('/admin/settings/rules', name: 'admin_settings_rules', methods: ['GET'])]
    public function index(): Response
    {
        $this->denyAccessUnlessGranted('ROLE_ADMIN');
        return new Response(<<<'HTML'
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Operational rules · Dulogix</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f7fb;color:#17314e;font:14px system-ui}main{max-width:950px;margin:25px auto;padding:0 16px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #dbe3ee;border-radius:10px;padding:20px;margin:14px 0}h1{font-size:26px}h2{font-size:18px;margin-top:0}li{margin:10px 0;line-height:1.5}.badge{display:inline-block;border-radius:5px;background:#fff0d0;color:#754d00;padding:5px 9px;font-size:12px}a{color:#174a7d}.muted{color:#5a6b7d;line-height:1.5}</style></head><body><main><p><a href="/admin/settings">← Admin Settings</a></p><h1>Dulogix operational rules</h1><p class="muted">Documented business rules. This page is read-only and does not activate functionality.</p><section class="card"><h2>Understanding the rota stages</h2><p>Each Monday–Sunday rota moves through four stages. The label describes <strong>what the selected week is being used for</strong>, rather than simply whether it is in the past or future.</p><ol><li><strong>🟡 Planning:</strong> Next week’s rota is being prepared. Managers can allocate drivers, update availability and complete Weekly Operations Planning.</li><li><strong>🟢 Live Rota:</strong> This is the week drivers are currently working. It stays editable so managers can respond to sickness, unexpected unavailability and operational changes.</li><li><strong>🟠 Review Period:</strong> Last week’s rota remains editable for the <strong>entire following Monday–Sunday week</strong>, allowing final corrections and reconciliation.</li><li><strong>🔒 Locked:</strong> At <strong>00:00 UK time on the Monday after the review week</strong>, the completed rota becomes read-only. A manager can still make an audited correction using a temporary unlock.</li></ol><p class="muted"><strong>Example:</strong> The rota for 26 October–1 November 2026 is Live Rota during those dates, Review Period from 2–8 November, and Locked from Monday 9 November at 00:00 UK time. The rota for 2–8 November is Planning during the preceding week.</p><p class="muted">These stages apply to driver availability, allocations, statuses, Weekly Operations Planning and Weekly Actions. PDF export and viewing remain available after locking.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Historical rota locking and corrections</h2><p><span class="badge">Implemented locally · Pending end-to-end verification and deployment</span></p><ol><li><strong>Scope:</strong> Lock all edits to driver availability, allocations, statuses, Weekly Operations Planning and Weekly Actions for the selected historical week. Viewing and PDF export remain available.</li><li><strong>When:</strong> A completed Monday–Sunday rota remains editable throughout the entire following review week. It automatically locks at <strong>00:00 on the second Monday after its Sunday end date, Europe/London time</strong>.</li><li><strong>Manager unlock:</strong> An authorised manager can unlock the selected historical week without administrator approval or email. The interface must show an audit warning and require a reason before unlocking.</li><li><strong>Duration:</strong> Unlock lasts at most 30 minutes. The manager can relock early. The server must reject edits after expiry.</li><li><strong>Access:</strong> Only the manager who initiated the unlock can edit during that session; other users remain read-only.</li><li><strong>Audit:</strong> Display a Historical Week Audit accordion on the rota page recording unlocks, reasons, actor, time, relocks and every historical correction with before/after values across all sections.</li><li><strong>Retention:</strong> Keep historical unlock/relock events and corrections for 12 months. Ordinary rota change history remains at 3 months.</li><li><strong>Validation:</strong> Historical corrections must still respect normal rota validation rules, including the six-consecutive-driving-days limit.</li></ol><p class="muted">Locking and audit must be enforced server-side, not just by disabling page controls. No email notification or approval workflow is required.</p></section><section class="card"><h2>Permanent account roles</h2><p>Each account is created as an <strong>Administrator, Manager or Driver</strong>. Its account role is permanent and cannot be changed from the Edit User page or through a modified form submission.</p><ul><li>If a Driver becomes a Manager (or vice versa), create a <strong>new account with a unique username</strong>. Deactivate the original Driver account rather than deleting it, preserving rota and availability history.</li><li>Driver operational type may still change between <strong>Driver and Jumper</strong> without changing the account role.</li><li>Administrators may continue to change a Manager’s assigned <strong>Rota Management</strong> and <strong>Vehicle Management</strong> sections.</li><li>Separate accounts may use the <strong>same email address</strong>, but usernames must remain unique. No email notification is required.</li></ul></section><section class="card"><h2>Related policy</h2><p>See <a href="/admin/settings/retention">Data retention policy</a> for the agreed storage and deletion periods.</p></section></main></body></html>
HTML);
    }
